    {
      "id": "s21",
      "start": 162.12,
      "end": 170.36,
      "narration": "It's fast, it's cheap, and the intelligence is dangerously close to top tier closed models. But how did they make an open source model run this fast without melting the hardware?",
      "intent": "brand-group",
      "intensity": "medium",
      "assets": [
        "logos/chatgpt.svg",
        "logos/claude.svg",
        "logos/gemini.svg",
        "logos/grok.svg"
      ],
      "animations": [
        {
          "id": "A28",
          "params": {
            "names": [
              "ChatGPT",
              "Claude",
              "Gemini",
              "Grok"
            ],
            "files": [
              "chatgpt.svg",
              "claude.svg",
              "gemini.svg",
              "grok.svg"
            ],
            "highlight": -1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A40",
          "params": {
            "label": "PARITY"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A32",
          "params": {
            "label": "Melt Hardware?"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "start": 170.36,
      "end": 177.56,
      "narration": "The secret isn't just raw computing power. It's a masterclass in systems engineering. Normally when you send a massive prompt to an AI, like an entire software code base,",
      "intent": "title",
      "intensity": "hero",
      "assets": [],
      "animations": [
        {
          "id": "A01",
          "params": {
            "title": "Systems Engineering",
            "subtitle": "How DeepSeek achieved peak throughput",
            "icon": "chip"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A04",
          "params": {
            "title": "Massive Prompt",
            "lines": [
              "Full repository",
              "Millions of tokens"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A38",
          "params": {
            "before": "Secret is",
            "word": "Architecture",
            "after": "not brute force"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "start": 177.56,
      "end": 185.48,
      "narration": "the model has to process every single word through every single layer of its network before it can write the very first letter. That reading phase eats up an enormous amount of compute.",
      "intent": "layers",
      "intensity": "medium",
      "assets": [],
      "animations": [
        {
          "id": "A20",
          "params": {
            "layers": [
              "Layer 1..32",
              "Attention Pass",
              "Layer 33..64"
            ],
            "highlight": 1,
            "note": "All Layers Pass"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A18",
          "params": {
            "gate": "ALL LAYERS"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A51",
          "params": {
            "from": "Full Reading",
            "to": "Heavy Compute"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "start": 185.48,
      "end": 195.56,
      "narration": "DeepSeek solved this at the architectural level by splitting their layers in half using a causal encoder/decoder design. The bottom layers act as a dedicated reader while the top layers act as a writer.",
      "intent": "compare",
      "intensity": "hero",
      "assets": [],
      "animations": [
        {
          "id": "A11",
          "params": {
            "left": "Monolith Model",
            "right": "Causal Split"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A22",
          "params": {
            "layers": [
              "Reader Layers",
              "Causal Bridge",
              "Writer Layers"
            ],
            "highlight": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A10",
          "params": {
            "left": "Bottom: Reader",
            "right": "Top: Writer"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "start": 195.56,
      "end": 204.36,
      "narration": "When your prompt comes in, it only runs through half the layers, cutting the heavy reading work in half before the server even breaks a sweat. On top of that, they use wide expert parallelism.",
      "intent": "sequence",
      "intensity": "medium",
      "assets": [],
      "animations": [
        {
          "id": "A14",
          "params": {
            "labels": [
              "Prompt In",
              "Half Layers",
              "Fast Start"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A25",
          "params": {
            "values": [
              100,
              50
            ],
            "labels": [
              "Before",
              "After"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "A02",
          "params": {
            "before": "Deploying",
            "keyword": "Wide MoE"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "start": 204.36,
      "end": 212.76,
      "narration": "Instead of forcing one GPU to carry all the weight, they distribute the AI's experts across clusters of 64 to 128 graphics cards.",
      "intent": "hierarchy",
      "intensity": "hero",
      "assets": [],
      "animations": [
        {
          "id": "A24",
          "params": {
            "root": "Wide MoE Cluster",
            "children": [
              "64-128 GPUs",
              "Shared Memory",
              "Expert Nodes"
